                            <comment id="16783140" author="vozerov" created="Mon, 4 Mar 2019 09:09:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=tledkov-gridgain&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;tledkov-gridgain&quot;&gt;tledkov-gridgain&lt;/a&gt;, looks good to me in general, but I am not quite understand &lt;tt&gt;JdbcRequestHandler.OrderedBatchWorker#body&lt;/tt&gt; method: why do we do &lt;tt&gt;peek&lt;/tt&gt; and then make &lt;tt&gt;poll&lt;/tt&gt;? Can we just make one &lt;tt&gt;poll&lt;/tt&gt; instead?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16783167" author="tledkov-gridgain" created="Mon, 4 Mar 2019 09:41:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=vozerov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;vozerov&quot;&gt;vozerov&lt;/a&gt;, because It is possible that the queue dosn&apos;t contain the request with expected order.&lt;br/&gt;
In this case we can do &lt;tt&gt;poll / add&lt;/tt&gt; to return the request to queue or do &lt;tt&gt;peek / poll&lt;/tt&gt; and poll only expected message.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16784170" author="vozerov" created="Tue, 5 Mar 2019 07:09:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=tledkov-gridgain&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;tledkov-gridgain&quot;&gt;tledkov-gridgain&lt;/a&gt;, got it. In order to proceed please confirm that mentioned JavaDoc and Licence Headers suites are ok. At the very least I see missing header in &lt;tt&gt;JdbcThinStreamingResetStreamTest&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
